        {
            "id": 41,
            "documentId": "du85yojsaac5r8jh877kjgl1",
            "title": "Reflections in the Midnight Oil",
            "content": "When the golden hour has passed, the lesser light of the patient cosmos soon emerges in her course. Her magnificence is perched in her dark dominion, high in the heavens amidst scintillating halos. With a gentle touch, she begins her nightly conquest anew, loosening her milky satin glow upon the cold earth.\n\nThe fervor of restless men who burn up all on the inside drowses,\n\nFervor drowses as restless men burn up all on the inside, rising into the descending black. Like a babe hushed at his mother's breast, a still of the night is nurtured in the sibylline sootfall...\n\nRestless men burn, fervor dies without aim, and like a babe hushed at his mother's breast, a still of the night is nurtured in the sweet, sibylline sootfall...\n\nThe restless man tucked away in his quiet nook knows this well and as a matter of course is bemused little. What is it worth to pay any mind to what is sure and sure to follow? Pragmatism be damned if he were to heavily consider such things, allowing them to hamper his routine toil. The greatest of thinkers have long ago done their worthwhile work; a mountain looming shadow over his eyes, every day as his mind wanders, constantly sobering him to the mundane. Perhaps in more youthful days an air of romanticism was essential in his perception of the world around him. Could it be even supplemental now that he is grown and dignification is his cause? Well, upon reflection, the annals of his short history illustrate profusely that by the abstract means of this sole focus it shall not be truly fulfilled.\n\nIn large part this is due to the settled mindedness of the limits of his understanding. But a settled mindedness is not an entitlement, nor a virtue for men, but a sad illusion as they know nothing. The way by which this degradation has festered is irrelevant, only that expansion of his mind is halted and a self-inflicted stagnation is achieved in the stead of dignity. A continual failed mission of his own making. Little by little this has occurred, without concern for the moon or the sky or the wind or the trees. What now can be said of his soul?",
            "createdAt": "2025-04-04T19:50:57.586Z",
            "updatedAt": "2025-10-30T23:33:46.875Z",
